    "crystal_structure": "Para-aramid: linear, rod-like chains (amide linkages at para/1,4 ring positions) pack into a highly extended, hydrogen-bonded crystalline structure, giving exceptional axial strength and stiffness. Meta-aramid (1,3 linkages) is less linear and used more for heat/flame resistance than pure tensile strength. PPTA unit cell: monoclinic (pseudo-orthorhombic), a:b:c = 0.78:0.519:1.29 nm, 2 chains/cell (Wypych, Mark).",
